<media><image src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/b5550b7a3872186a47c5c9c5fc3fc821acf47068"/>
</media><para>Algebra 1 by OpenStax is licensed under Creative Commons Attribution License v4.0. Algebra 1 was authored by OpenStax and is based, in part, on OpenStax Prealgebra, Elementary Algebra, Intermediate Algebra, and College Algebra materials, and the IM 6–12 Math™ by Illustrative Mathematics®.  </para>
<para class="os-raise-text-center">
  <media><image src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/c2341a199132c97f4e9fa2b46af32f93effa291b"/>
  </media><media><image src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/b98c2ee691d1230e7411c276dee1ad1666791c21"/>

</media></para>
<title>Senior Contributing Authors:
</title>
<title class="os-raise-indent">Lynn Marecek, Santa Ana College
</title>
<title class="os-raise-indent">MaryAnne Anthony-Smith, Formerly of Santa Ana College
</title>
<title class="os-raise-indent">Andrea Honeycutt Mathis, Northeast Mississippi Community College
</title>
<title class="os-raise-indent">Jay Abramson, Arizona State University
</title>
<title class="os-raise-indent">Sharon North, St. Louis Community College
</title>
<title class="os-raise-indent">Amy Baldwin, University of Central Arkansas
</title>
<para>Algebra 1 was authored by OpenStax and is based, in part, on the OpenStax Prealgebra, Elementary Algebra, Intermediate Algebra, and College Algebra materials, and the IM 6–12 Math™ by Illustrative Mathematics®. Based on OpenStax’s open (CC-BY) license, educators may remix and reuse the elements and content in Algebra 1 according to their approach. OpenStax textbooks are always free online.</para>
<para>All OpenStax textbooks undergo a rigorous review process. However, like any professional-grade textbook, errors sometimes occur. If you have a correction to suggest, submit it to k12@openstax.org. We review your suggestions and make the necessary changes.
</para>

<media><image src="https://k12.openstax.org/contents/raise/resources/b98c2ee691d1230e7411c276dee1ad1666791c21"/>
</media><para>Students who don’t complete Algebra 1 have just a 1 in 5 chance of graduating from high school. Increasing access to rigorous, engaging, standards-aligned Algebra content helps prepare more students to succeed in higher-level mathematics. 
</para>

<list>
  <item>Algebra 1 is a critical “gateway course” in K12 education. 
  </item>
  <item>Success in Algebra 1 is a predictor of on-time graduation rates, success in higher-level mathematics, and post-secondary success. 
  </item>
  <item>OpenStax Algebra 1 is a High-Quality Instructional Material designed for secondary Algebra instruction. 
  </item>
</list>
<para>OpenStax Algebra 1 is a complete Algebra 1 curriculum and an open education resource (OER) that is standards-aligned, easy to implement, supportive of diverse learners, and engaging for students. Algebra 1 is supported by instructional support resources, including implementation guidance, pacing suggestions, and ancillary engagement materials.
</para>
<para>ISBN: 978-1-961584-47-1 </para>
